Z||000006||Slammed Fiero||05-09-2001||08:56 PM||||Who cares , they drive RX-7's. Actually who cares what they drive. We just look like morons if we go on every mailing list defending our cars to people who aren't worth the time. People who are to ignorant to read up on the matter before they post verbal diareah<P>and in closing , a fellow autocrosser Rick potter , top 5 finisher at the One lap of america and participant for the last few years in the event has replaced the motor on his RX-7 more times than can be counted , seals blow all the time , he swears at the car a lot , a twin turbo motor costs $15,000 Canadian. <P>JM<P>DOH!!<P><p>[This message has been edited by Slammed Fiero (edited 05-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||Jay||05-09-2001||09:59 PM||||I have to agree, most import guys find what we do to fiero's as cool.  I'm involved not only in Fiero clubs but also import clubs.  They've welcomed me in with open arms.  I've gotta admit, some Hondas will kick my V8's ass in the 1/4 mile, but it's all good.  Darknights, Team Evolution and others all accept the Fiero as a genuine modern Hot Rod.  And that's all I've got to say about that!<P>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT <A HREF="http://www.members.home.net/jaygrande" TARGET=_blank>www.members.home.net/jaygrande</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||88formula||05-09-2001||10:15 PM||||Trying to convince the rx7 guys or any other car owners than the fiero is a great sports car is too much work. They love their cars and we love ours and you cant tell them otherwise. <P>I could bang my head against the wall for three hours and accomplish the same thing as trying to convince them.<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
